      "note": {
        "title": "Later Reporting on Undisclosed Variants at WIV",
        "html": "<p>According to subsequent reporting by the Sunday Times, the Wuhan Institute of Virology had been working with undisclosed variants from the Mojiang mine. At least one of these unpublished strains was believed to be an even closer genetic match to SARS-CoV-2 than RaTG13. As one investigator stated: “We are confident they were working on a closer unpublished variant — possibly collected in Mojiang” (<a href=\"?chapter=19\">Chapter 19</a> <em><a href=\"?source=ch19-s16\">Calvert & Arbuthnott 2023</a></em>).</p>",
